    "key": "svc.p007",
    "en": "One contact with one person",
    "html": false,
    "page": "contact.html"
  },
  {
    "key": "svc.p008",
    "en": "Use this when you have seen, spoken to or supported a specific person. For a group activity or a day's total, use the <a href=\"5ws-report.html\">activity report</a> instead — this form is deliberately one record per person per contact, because that is the only way a returning person can be recognised instead of counted twice.",
    "html": true,
    "page": "contact.html"
  },
  {
    "key": "svc.p009",
    "en": "<b>The person's name and phone number stay on this handset.</b> You type a few details so the phone can work out a <b>contact code</b>; the details are used for that calculation and then discarded. Only the code is saved. Nobody downstream — not the coordination view, not the dashboard, not this site — ever receives the name, the number, or a date of birth.",
    "html": true,
    "page": "contact.html"
  },
  {
    "key": "svc.p010",
    "en": "<b>Works with no signal.</b> Records are held on this phone as you save them and sent to the coordination register on their own when there is signal. The export remains for a copy of your own. <span id=\"storeWarn\"></span>",
    "html": true,
    "page": "contact.html"
  },
  {
